-- title:
--   Compositum of level M/p q-expansions and their q↦ qᵖ translates
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing the kernel of reduction, i.e. every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $M/p \mid M$ is $1$ lies in $H$. Write $H' =$ `infSubgroup p M H hpM` for the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ under that same reduction map on units. For a pair $(N, K)$ consisting of a level and a subgroup, `xHFunctionFieldBar N K` denotes `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (xHFunctionFieldC ℚ N K)`, that is, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the field `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ N K` of rational $q$-expansions attached to $(N,K)$. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the join (compositum) of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) H'` with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield generated by the image of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) H'` under the ring homomorphism `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p`, which rescales the exponent support by $p$, so $\sum a_n q^n \mapsto \sum a_n q^{pn}$, equals `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`.
--
--   This identifies the function field at level $M$ (in its $q$-expansion realisation over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) as the compositum of the images of the two degeneracy maps from level $M/p$, under the hypothesis that $H$ contains the kernel of reduction modulo $M/p$, which forces $\Gamma_H(M) = \Gamma_{H'}(M/p) \cap \Gamma_0(M)$. It is the tool by which $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra maps on the level-$M$ function field are pinned down by their effect on level-$M/p$ functions and their $q \mapsto q^p$ translates, and is used in the project to verify commutation and norm relations for diamond automorphisms and for the Atkin–Lehner involution.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_xHFunctionFieldBar_div_sup_adjoin_qExpand_eq_xHFunctionFieldBar.lean

